# Ascribe 1: the MiniCOSM for a person's holograph (Ascribe: a self described well enough that no name is needed).
#
# What a program needs to know to read a holograph: a folder whose catalog, holograph.cosm, is the self, declared
# oes: ascribe/1, with a pseudonymous handle and no name of the person anywhere. Beside the catalog sit ten module
# folders, one kind each, the kind the singular of the module's name and the letter its initial: A affinity, B belief,
# C concern, E experience, I interest, O opinion, Q quale, S skill, U understanding, Y yearning. Every node of the self
# is one of these ten kinds, and every node anchors to a form. The forms live in F: anything a person can love or
# hate, know well or want to learn (is there an encyclopedia article for it, or should there be?), grounded in FEED
# where the form is one word that FEED has, with the polyforms that combine them and the relations an author declares.
# The rest is the author's to shape as they go: hierarchies, branches and flat lists by parts and of, typed links from
# a short starter list or from relations they declare, a when, a valence and a strength. The dialectic: block holds
# the bank of opening questions the core's dialectic asks the holder (module D, beside the containers: the holder's
# own words, which never leave); the moves: block declares propose, which reads the holder's own text for candidate
# nodes that become the holder's only by their answer.
#
# The prose is Ascribe, the canonical edition at https://ascribe.cosmoes.org/ (bundled as docs/ASCRIBE.md); this
# file is its machine-readable declaration. The reference reader is enough/macrocosm.py; Ascribe's own checks are
# enough/ascribe.py. Where this file and the reader disagree, one of them is in error and is corrected.
#
# No personal data, three ways: the schema has no kind or field for it; the no-pii check warns, and never refuses
# inside the holograph, on what reads like it (at a projection it is an error); and the filter: block keeps private
# files, restricted items and module D out of everything that leaves.
#
# Written in the COSM YAML subset: no anchors, no aliases, no tags, one document. Words that YAML 1.1 reads as
# booleans (on, off, yes, no) are quoted.
#
# Copyright © 2026 Graham Smith. All rights reserved. See defaults/cosm/NOTICE.md.

manifest: minicosm/0
macrocosm: 0.6.0
name: ascribe
title: Ascribe
version: 1
summary: "A person's holograph: a self described in ten kinds of node, each anchored to a form, comprehensive enough that a name is unnecessary."
spec: https://ascribe.cosmoes.org/    # Ascribe, the canonical edition (bundled as docs/ASCRIBE.md)
reference: [enough/macrocosm.py, enough/ascribe.py]

declaration:
  key: oes
  value: ascribe/1
  absent: refuse                  # a holograph.cosm without oes: ascribe/1 is refused
  legacy: []
  both: oes
  unknown: refuse

format:
  extension: .cosm
  syntax: the COSM YAML subset
  forbidden: [anchors, aliases, tags, multiple documents]
  booleans: ['true', 'false']
  encoding: utf-8
  byte-order-mark: tolerated
  newlines: [lf, crlf]

# Laid out as a Holotype's atoms are, minus the parts level: one person, one volume, so the module folders sit directly
# beside the catalog. The reader reads every module file below the catalog's folder; enough/ascribe.py holds each node
# to its own module's folder (check id-module), and the catalog may carry a few nodes of any module in its own nodes:.
volume:
  catalog: holograph.cosm
  modules: <module>/              # A/ B/ C/ E/ I/ O/ Q/ S/ U/ Y/ for the ten kinds; F/ for forms, polyforms, relations; D/ for the dialectic's questions and sessions
  module-files: '<module folder>/**/*.cosm'
  module-folder-case: read either, write the capital
  private-marker: .ascribe-private  # see filter: below

catalog:
  keys: [oes, macrocosm, id, handle, summary, subject, sample, visibility, pseudonyms, releases, morphs, nodes]
  id: ascribe/<hid>               # ascribe/aej6l5qrka6c6btarfiy2f7vnj
  hid: '[a-z2-7]{26}'             # 26 characters of lowercase base32, as Connect's hid; checked by enough/ascribe.py
  handle: 'a pseudonymous handle: lowercase words joined by hyphens (salt-and-crumb); never a name'
  summary: one line, optional; people appear in it by role, never by name
  subject: [person, character]    # person when absent: the holder's own self; character: the self of a subject that is not a person (a character, a persona, an agent run by a model), kept by its holder; an agent lists only from a character's holograph
  subject-absent: person
  sample: [true, false]          # true on a fixture or a demonstration, never on a real person's holograph
  visibility: [public, internal, restricted]
  visibility-absent: internal
  pseudonyms: 'the stand-in names the author uses for the people in their life ("Wren", "the Captain"), so the
               no-pii check reads them as declared, not as personal names'
  releases: 'optional: every release the holder has made, oldest first, appended and never rewritten; each {epoch,
             as, program: {name, sha256}, trace: {run, sha256}, at, sha256, items} and, for a package''s graph.cosm,
             for: {path, sha256}; never what was withheld, a key, or the party a cryptograph was handed to (check
             release-shape)'
  release-as: [isograph, allograph, cryptograph, isomorph]
  release-as-withdrawn: [tokens]  # read in a record made before match-token lists were withdrawn; a writer makes none
  morphs: 'optional: the file names of the holder''s morph volumes, each a bare name ending .morph.cosm, kept beside
           the holograph''s folder and never inside it'
  never: [the person's name, an email address, a phone number, a postal address, a birth date, a government id,
          an employer's legal name]

module-file:
  shapes:
    - {key: nodes, holds: 'a list of items, each a mapping with a string id'}
  duplicate-id: load error, the first wins

ids:
  item-form: '<module>:<kind>/<slug>'
  node: '<module>:<kind>/<slug>, the kind the module''s one kind: A:affinity/sourdough-baking, Q:quale/starter-smell'
  form: 'F:form/<slug>, F:polyform/<slug>, F:relation/<slug>'
  inside-own-volume: bare

paths:
  form: '<module>/<kind>/<slug>#<field>'
  levels: [module, kind, item, field]
  segments:
    module: '[ABCEIOQSUYF]'
    kind: '[a-z][a-z0-9-]*'
    slug: '[A-Za-z0-9](?:[A-Za-z0-9._@-]*[A-Za-z0-9_@-])?'
    field: '[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]*(?:\.[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]*|\[[0-9]+\])*'
  map:
    - {path: '<module>', id: none}
    - {path: '<module>/<kind>', id: none}
    - {path: '<module>/<kind>/<slug>', id: '<module>:<kind>/<slug>'}
    - {path: '<item path>#<field>', id: none}
  qualified: 'oes:ascribe/<hid>/<path>'
  qualified-database: the catalog id without ascribe/
  case: kept and significant
  refused: [a leading slash, a trailing slash, an empty segment, '.', '..', percent-encoding, a backslash, whitespace, a colon,
            non-ASCII or control characters, a segment ending in a dot, a second '#', a kind the module does not declare,
            more than three segments, 'a Windows reserved name as any segment, in any case, alone or before a dot (con, con.txt, prn, aux, nul, com0-9, lpt0-9)']

# Comprise's envelope, so Thym moves work on both subjects: confidence and sources live in provenance, as they do in
# Comprise outside P. name is the item's, never the person's. form, of, parts, when, valence and strength are Ascribe's.
envelope:
  fields: [id, type, name, summary, status, visibility, provenance, pending, links, span, form, of, parts, when, valence,
           strength, made]
  references: [links]
  required: [id, type, name, summary, provenance]
  status: [active, dormant, planned, retired]   # retired: once true of the person, no longer (a belief given up)
  visibility: [public, internal, restricted]
  visibility-absent: internal
  provenance:
    fields: [mode, sources, confidence, state]
    modes: [dialectic, net-scan, system-scan, integration, structured-intake, manual, derived, asserted, archetype,
            catalogue, directory, accounting]
    states: [known, pending, not-disclosed, stale]
    state-default: known
    confidence: a number from 0 to 1, how sure the person is
    sources: 'a dialectic session (D:session/session-3, or the earlier spelling session-3), a text the author wrote
              (notes.md#L3-L7, or notes.md#sha256:<digest> for a candidate read from it), or self for what they wrote
              down directly'
    answered: 'kept like any unknown field: the session and confidence of each field an answer filled'
  span: '{lines: "12-18"} or {start: "<up to 60 characters>", end: "<up to 60 characters>"}, optional: where in a
         text the node was read'
  form: 'F:form/<slug> or F:polyform/<slug>: what the node is about; every node of the ten kinds carries one (check
         form-anchored)'
  of: the node this one is a child of; the parent lists it in parts
  parts: the node's children, in order; a hierarchy, a branch or a flat list, as the author likes
  when: 'a date (2014-06-03), a year (2014) or an era word (childhood, 2010s, university); absent, the node is not on
         the timeline (check when-shape)'
  valence: 'for, against or mixed: an affinity against something is still an affinity'
  strength: a whole number from 1 to 5 (check strength-range)
  made: '{move, run, step, engine}: the Thym move that made the item; {move: none} for a hand-made item (docs/THYM.md
         5.3); a generic reader keeps it as an unknown field'
  metadata: on a form it is global, shared by every node anchored to it; on a node it belongs to that node alone
  open-question: '{pending: "<the question>"}'
  withheld: 'kept like any unknown field: the fields the holder declined to answer'
  sentinels: [none, self]
  unknown-fields: allowed and kept

# The starter relations. links.rels is left out on purpose: a closed list there would make the generic reader refuse a
# relation an author declares. relation-declared, Ascribe's own check, closes the list instead: a rel is a starter
# word, or the slug (or the id) of an F:relation the holograph declares, and nothing else, so a typo never becomes a
# relation.
links:
  starter: [is-a, part-of, about, because, before, after, with, against, like, from, toward, see]
  declared: 'F:relation/<slug>, with a name and a one-line summary giving its sense; a link names it as rel: <slug>'
  order: before and after order nodes in time without dates

closed-lists:
  valence: [for, against, mixed]
  feed.origin: [feed, user]

references:
  forms:
    - {form: bare, example: 'F:form/sourdough', names: an item of the same holograph}
    - {form: typed-link, example: '{rel: because, to: E:experience/first-night-crossing}',
       names: its to; rel a starter word or a declared relation}
    - {form: open-question, example: '{pending: "<question>"}', names: an answer still owed}
  unresolved: error
  other-people: 'never a reference to another person''s holograph: what one person knows of another is an experience
                 in their own'

modules:
  A:
    name: Affinities
    subtitle: What you are drawn to, and what you turn from
    kinds:
      affinity: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  B:
    name: Beliefs
    subtitle: What you hold to be true
    kinds:
      belief: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  C:
    name: Concerns
    subtitle: What weighs on you
    kinds:
      concern: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  E:
    name: Experiences
    subtitle: What has happened to you, and what you did
    kinds:
      experience: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  I:
    name: Interests
    subtitle: What you want to know more about
    kinds:
      interest: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  O:
    name: Opinions
    subtitle: What you think, and would say so
    kinds:
      opinion: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  Q:
    name: Qualia
    subtitle: How things feel from the inside
    kinds:
      quale: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  S:
    name: Skills
    subtitle: What you can do
    kinds:
      skill: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  U:
    name: Understandings
    subtitle: What you have come to understand
    kinds:
      understanding: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  Y:
    name: Yearnings
    subtitle: What you long for
    kinds:
      yearning: {refs: [form, of, parts, links], checked: [when, valence, strength]}
  F:
    name: Forms
    subtitle: The things a self is about, and how they combine
    note: forms are shared roots, not nodes of the self; they anchor nothing and need no form of their own
    kinds:
      # form: feed is {word, pos, origin: feed|user} when the form is one word FEED has, else {pending: "not in FEED"};
      # wiki is a URL or an article's title. polyform: forms are the forms it combines; links, {from, rel, to}, join them.
      form: {refs: [links], checked: [feed, wiki, when]}
      polyform: {refs: [forms, links, links.from], checked: [feed, wiki, when]}
      relation: {refs: [], checked: [name, summary]}         # a relation the author declares; links name it by its slug

checks:
  load: [load]
  envelope: [duplicate-id, id-grammar, id-module, type, type-prefix, identity-min, provenance, status, visibility, ref-grammar,
             ref-unresolved, closed-list, pending-shape, catalog-key]
  own: 'Ascribe''s own checks, run by enough/ascribe.py (lint_holograph) after the generic ones; a generic reader does not run
        them. form-anchored: every node of the ten kinds names a form or a polyform that exists. relation-declared: every
        link''s rel is a starter word or a relation the holograph declares. when-shape: a when is a date, a year or an
        era word. strength-range: a strength is a whole number from 1 to 5. release-shape: every releases entry has the
        fields a release requires, its as, epoch and digests in their shape, and every morphs entry is a bare file name
        ending .morph.cosm. no-pii: an email address, a phone number, an id-like run of digits, a street address, a date
        that reads as a birth, a field for any of these, or a capitalised pair in a prose field that reads as a personal
        name, anywhere in the volume, comments included; a warning inside the holograph, never an error there, and an
        error at a projection, which is refused while it stands. private-marker: what a .ascribe-private marker would
        keep out of everything that leaves, a note. form-anchored holds the ten kinds only, never an item of D. The same
        code also holds id-module to the module folders and catalog-key to the hid and the handle, which the generic
        reader cannot read from this file. A holograph that carries module D also passes the dialectic''s checks
        (enough/fabula.py).'
  severity: {no-pii: warning}

open-questions:
  form: '{pending: "<the question>"}'
  answered-by: the person; a dialectic may ask it again later
  field-path: keys joined by ".", list positions as [n]
  on-the-whole-item: field path node

renderers:
  - id: self
    makes: the self at a glance, a branch for each module and a leaf for each node
    lens: {kind: mermaid, diagram: mindmap, include: [A, B, C, E, I, O, Q, S, U, Y]}
  - id: timeline
    makes: every node that carries a when, one row each, dates and years in order and eras after them
    lens: {kind: table, columns: [when, id, name, valence, strength]}
  - id: graph
    makes: every typed link between the nodes and the forms, coloured by valence
    lens: {kind: mermaid, diagram: flowchart, include: [A, B, C, E, I, O, Q, S, U, Y, F], edges: [links], class-by: valence,
           shape: {form: '([ ])', polyform: '{{ }}', relation: '[/ /]'}}
  - {id: text-tree, makes: the text tree, code: [python -m enough.macrocosm tree]}

# The bank ascribe: four opening questions for each module of the self and four for the forms, in plain words and in
# no one's voice, each asked of the holograph once (about: <letter>, kind: text, to: holder, why: missing; entry ids
# A1, A2 … by position, so a question raised from the first says raised.from: ascribe/A1). The core's dialectic asks
# them (module D, enough/dialectic.py, through enough/ascribe.py); settle writes an answer as a node in the question's
# container, or for a question of the forms a form, anchored as follow-ups: and writes: say.
dialectic:
  status: applied; the core's questions and sessions in module D, D/ beside the containers (Ascribe, section 8)
  to: holder
  writes: {A: 'A:affinity', B: 'B:belief', C: 'C:concern', E: 'E:experience', I: 'I:interest', O: 'O:opinion',
           Q: 'Q:quale', S: 'S:skill', U: 'U:understanding', Y: 'Y:yearning', F: 'F:form'}
  provenance: '{mode: dialectic, sources: [D:session/<id>], confidence: <how sure the person is; 1 when they gave none
               and stated it plainly>}; the earlier spelling session-<n> names D:session/session-<n> and stays valid'
  form-discovery: 'a form or polyform of the holograph the answer is plainly about; else a new form for one word FEED
                   has, feed: {word, pos, origin: feed}; else a new form whose feed is {pending: "not in FEED"}, named
                   in the holder''s words; an answer that names no thing at all writes no node, and a follow-up asks
                   what it is about'
  follow-ups:
    - {about: '#form', asks: 'What is this about, in a word or two?', kind: text}
    - {about: '#when', asks: 'When was this, roughly: a date, a year, or a time of life?', kind: date}
    - {about: '#valence', asks: 'Does this draw you, put you off, or both?', kind: choice, options: [for, against, mixed]}
    - {about: '#strength', asks: 'How strongly, from 1 to 5?', kind: number, range: [1, 5]}
  not-knowing: '"I don''t know" on a field leaves {pending: "<their words>"}; a refusal adds the field to withheld and
                sets provenance.state: not-disclosed; on a bank question neither writes anything, and a declined entry
                is not put again unless the holder asks'
  never-written: 'a name, an address or a government identifier: the answer is refused in plain words and the question
                  stays open'
  questions:
    A:
      - What do you go back to, again and again?
      - What can you not stand, even when everyone around you loves it?
      - Which place or kind of work feels most like yours?
      - What did you love as a child that you still love?
    B:
      - What do you believe that most people around you do not?
      - What did you once believe and no longer do?
      - What would you hold to even if it cost you something?
      - What do you take on trust?
    C:
      - What keeps you awake at night?
      - What do you worry about for the people close to you?
      - Which problem do you wish more people noticed?
      - If you could fix one thing, what would it be?
    E:
      - What happened that changed the direction of your life?
      - Which day would you live again?
      - What have you done that you are proud of?
      - Which stretch of years feels like a chapter of its own?
    I:
      - What could you read about for hours?
      - What have you looked up lately just because you wanted to know?
      - What would you study if you had a year to spare?
      - What do you notice that others walk past?
    O:
      - What do you think most people get wrong?
      - What is overrated, and what is underrated?
      - Which argument would you gladly start at dinner?
      - What have you changed your mind about lately?
    Q:
      - Which sensation do you remember most exactly?
      - What does your favourite weather feel like?
      - Which sound, smell or taste takes you straight back somewhere?
      - What does it feel like when your work is going well?
    S:
      - What can you do without thinking about it?
      - What do people ask you to help with?
      - What did you learn the hard way?
      - What are you getting better at right now?
    U:
      - What do you understand now that you did not ten years ago?
      - What could you explain to a curious stranger?
      - Which idea changed how you see things once it clicked?
      - What do you know from experience that no book taught you?
    Y:
      - What do you wish you had time for?
      - What would you try if you knew you could not fail?
      - Where would you go, given the chance?
      - What do you miss?
    F:
      - Which words would you put on a list of things you care about?
      - What would you look up first in an encyclopedia?
      - Which subject deserves an article that nobody has written yet?
      - Which things belong together for you, though others keep them apart?

# What leaves a holograph and what stays (Ascribe, section 11). enough/ascribe.py's private_filter applies it, a pure
# function of the folder, before anything else in each use reads the holograph; its private-marker check reports what
# a marker withholds, and withholds nothing.
filter:
  status: declared and applied (enough/ascribe.py private_filter)
  applies-to: [ingest, package, transfer, projection]
  marker: .ascribe-private
  drops:
    - every file and folder beside a .ascribe-private marker, with everything below them, the marker included; a marker beside the catalog withholds the whole holograph
    - every node, form, polyform, relation and dialectic item with visibility restricted, wherever it is written; a kept file that holds one is written out again without it, as its nodes in the COSM YAML subset, without its comments
    - module D, in every use but a transfer of the whole holograph into the holder's own keeping
  keeps: everything else, unchanged and byte for byte when its file holds nothing restricted; a reference to a withheld item keeps its id and gains no name; no placeholder or count; the catalog unless a marker sits beside it

# What may leave, by a Thym program the holder runs, after the filter, recorded as a release (Ascribe, sections 13
# and 14): default-deny; withhold, never falsify; nothing of the dialectic and nothing pending; no personal data, no-pii
# an error here. There is no paratype of a person. The isograph is for private sharing, handed by the holder to whom
# they choose; the allograph is the one thing of a holograph a registry lists, and only when its holder lists it.
public-projection:
  status: 'the isograph and the allograph, built (enough/ascribe.py project_isograph, project_allograph); the
           Allograph Registry''s client, keys and statements, built (enough/allograph_registry.py); further opt-in
           fields of an isograph are reserved for a later edition, for private sharing'
  isograph: an isograph is a Thym projection of the holograph, made by a program its holder runs (Thym, https://thym.cosmoes.org/), for private sharing; nothing lists, hosts or signs one
  schema: ascribe-isograph/0
  fields: [isograph, hid, handle, epoch, sample, program, run, self]
  self-fields: [kind, form, valence, strength, when, marking]
  marking: stated                 # verified is reserved for what a registry attests; a reader refuses an isograph carrying it
  derivable: []                   # Ascribe lists nothing as derivable, so mark ... as verified is refused over a holograph
  strength-bands: {slight: [1, 2], moderate: [3], strong: [4, 5]}
  when: the decade of a date or a year (2010s), or an era word already in that shape; any other era word is left out
  may-appear: 'a node of the ten kinds whose visibility is public, whose status is absent or active, whose provenance is
               known at confidence 0.5 or more, that the filter keeps, and whose form, or every form of whose polyform
               (at most eight), is grounded in FEED with origin feed'
  limits: {per-kind: 20, bytes: 65536}
  sorted: [module, form, valence, strength, when]
  per-epoch: 1
  canonical: JSON, keys sorted, no space between tokens, UTF-8 without a byte-order mark
  allograph: 'an allograph is a Thym projection of the holograph, made by project h as allograph: the holder''s public
              account of what they can do for others, listed in the Allograph Registry only at the holder''s word'
  allograph-schema: ascribe-allograph/0
  allograph-fields: [allograph, kind, epoch, sample, program, run, expertise]
  expertise-fields: [kind, form, strength, when, marking]
  allograph-kind: {person: person, character: agent}    # the catalog's subject gives the allograph's kind
  may-enter: 'a node of E, S or U (an experience, a skill, an understanding) whose visibility is public, whose status is
              absent or active, whose provenance is known at confidence 0.5 or more, whose valence is absent or for,
              that the filter keeps, and whose form, or every form of whose polyform (at most eight), is grounded in
              FEED with origin feed; never the other seven kinds, the handle, the hid, a name, a summary or any free text'
  allograph-entries: one per kind and form, with the strongest band and the latest decade among its nodes
  allograph-sorted: [module, form]
  allograph-per-epoch: any       # a holder may release more than one allograph in an epoch; made again, never edited
  cryptograph: 'a Thym package in its encrypted form of the filtered holograph (one holograph row per kept file, D left
                out) or of a projection (projection.json, program.thym, trace.cosm); a random hid; the key shown once;
                handed with its key to one chosen party, never hosted'
  tokens: 'withdrawn: the salted list ascribe-tokens/0 is made no more (a writer makes none; a release as tokens still
           reads); a search says what it needs as match tokens {about, value} (Ascribe, sections 14.3 and 14.11)'
  outsiders: no outsider's graph of a person exists

extension:
  status: 'the isograph, the allograph, the cryptograph and isomorphs are specified (Ascribe, section 14); the
           Allograph Registry replaces Ascribe-Connect and is the bridge to Comprise (sections 14.7 to 14.14)'
  note: an isograph and an allograph are each a Thym projection of the holograph; no outsider's graph of a person exists

# The moves Ascribe declares for Thym (Thym, https://thym.cosmoes.org/, sections 6.2, 6.3 and 17.6), for thym 1 only:
# propose, and the kinds it adds to project (isograph and allograph, in one entry; isotype and paratype stay Comprise
# OES's). propose asks the model; nothing it proposes is the holder's until they answer yes; a program lands it with
# gather. No move sends anything to a registry: listing an allograph is the implementation's act after the run.
moves:
  - name: propose
    takes: [fabula]
    gives: list of item
    modifiers: {with: volume}
    asks: true
    contract: [no-invention, provenance]
    code: enough.thym.moves.ascribe:propose
    says: candidate nodes a holder's own text suggests, each with the question that asks whether it is so
    since: 1
  - name: project
    extends: true
    takes: [volume]
    gives: volume
    modifiers: {as: 'isograph | allograph'}
